.TH SDL_NotificationAction 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_NotificationAction \- Notification structure describing actions that can be used to allow users to interact with notification dialogs.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_notification.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef union SDL_NotificationAction
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_NotificationActionType type;
.BI "
.BI "    struct
.BI "    {
.BI "        SDL_NotificationActionType type; /**< SDL_NOTIFICATION_ACTION_TYPE_BUTTON */
.BI "        const char *action_id;           /**< The identifier string for the button. 'default' is a reserved identifier and must not be used. */
.BI "        const char *action_label;        /**< The localized label for the button associated with the action, in UTF-8 encoding. */
.BI "    } button;
.BI "
.BI "    Uint8 padding[128];
.BI "} SDL_NotificationAction;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Exactly How they are presented depends on the platform and implementation\[char46]
.PP
User interactions with a notification are reported via events with the type
.BR SDL_EVENT_NOTIFICATION_ACTION_INVOKED \[char46]
.PP
Action types: - button: A button with a localized text label, which generates feedback when activated\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_NotificationEvent (3type),
.BR SDL_NotificationActionType (3)
